  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Common verbs with «essere»",
   "texto": [
    "Many frequent verbs of movement or change form the prossimo passage with **essere**: **andare** → andato, **venire** → venuto, **arrivare** → arrival, **partire** → partito, **uscire** (exit) → uscito, **tornare** (return) → tornado, **rimanere** (stay) → **rimasto**. It is not enough for a verb to indicate movement to decide the auxiliary: learn which auxiliary uses each frequent verb.",
    "All reflexive verbs form this time with **essere**: **Mi sono alzato** (I got up)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Conformity",
   "texto": [
    "With «essere», the participle matches the subject, as an adjective: **andato** (it), **andata** (it), **andati** (them), **andate** (them).",
    "A woman says **Sono andata**; two women, **Siamo andate**. In Italian this **sí se oye** when speaking."
